Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-04-23
Subject: Give bootstrap-only helper types explicit names
License: expat

The compiler sources lean on a few anonymous enums, record types, and
array-index declarations that are legal in FPC but awkward for the
bootstrap translator to lower directly.  These changes keep the same
types, but give them explicit names or ranges so the generated C++ sees
the same structure more directly.

--- a/compiler/i386/daopt386.pas
+++ b/compiler/i386/daopt386.pas
@@ -79,7 +79,7 @@
 {the possible states of a flag}
   TFlagContents = (F_Unknown, F_notSet, F_Set);
 
-  TContent = Packed Record
+  TContent = Record
       {start and end of block instructions that defines the
        content of this register.}
                StartMod: tai;
--- a/compiler/i386/ra386int.pas
+++ b/compiler/i386/ra386int.pas
@@ -118,7 +118,7 @@
